12:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-custom max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["# Mobile Email Optimization: Designing for the Small Screen in 2026"]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Excerpt:"}]," Over 60% of emails are opened on mobile devices. This guide covers responsive design, touch-friendly CTAs, and email preheader optimization -- with real-world benchmarks, 2026-specific best practices, and actionable steps you can implement *today*."]}],["$","hr","4",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["In 2026, mobile isn't just *a channel* for email -- it's the *primary interface*. According to Litmus' 2025 State of Email Report (released Q4 2025), ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"63.2% of all global email opens occurred on smartphones"}],", up from 58.7% in 2023. Tablets accounted for another 5.1%, meaning ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"nearly 7 in 10 email interactions begin on a small screen"}],". Yet, a 2026 Email Monday audit of 1,200 B2C marketing emails found that ",["$","strong","5",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"41% failed basic mobile rendering tests"}],", resulting in broken layouts, unreadable text, or unclickable buttons."]}],["$","p","8",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["If your email looks great on desktop but collapses into chaos on an iPhone 15 Pro or Samsung Galaxy S24 -- you're not just losing aesthetics. You're losing conversions, trust, and revenue."]}],["$","p","10",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Here's how to future-proof your email program for the mobile-first reality of 2026."]}],["$","hr","12",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","h2","14",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"✅ 1. Responsive Design: Beyond \"Fluid Width\""}],["$","p","16",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Gone are the days when setting `width=\"100%\"` on a table was enough. In 2026, true responsiveness means *adaptive behavior*, not just flexible sizing."]}],["$","h3","18",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"🔑 Key 2026 Requirements:"}],["$","p","19",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Single-column layouts only"}],": Multi-column grids (e.g., 2-up product carousels) still break in Apple Mail and Gmail Android. Use `<table>`-based fluid containers *or* hybrid coding (CSS media queries + fallbacks) -- but always test in Litmus' new \"iOS 18.4 + Gmail App v2026.12\" preview mode."]}],["$","p","20",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Font scaling that respects OS settings"}],": iOS 18 and Android 15 now enforce system-wide font scaling (up to 150%). Ensure body text is ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"minimum 16px"}],", headings no smaller than 22px -- and *never* use `font-size: 1rem` without a `min-font-size: 16px` fallback."]}],["$","p","21",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Image optimization"}],": 72% of mobile users abandon emails that take >3 seconds to load (Akamai, 2025). Compress hero images to <120KB using WebP (supported in all major email clients as of Q1 2026), and always include `height=\"auto\"` and `width=\"100%\"`."]}],"$L16","$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37","$L38","$L39","$L3a","$L3b","$L3c","$L3d","$L3e","$L3f","$L40","$L41","$L42","$L43","$L44","$L45","$L46","$L47","$L48","$L49","$L4a"]}]
